        "original_id": "8bbd19d1-aac9-56db-993a-206316d1f348",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Pratt Family Camps, Squam Lake, New Hampshire, White Mountains, Grafton County, Carroll County, Belknap County\n- Topics: camp buildings, lakefront property\n\nFacts:\n- Squam Lake is a lake in the Lakes Region of central New Hampshire, United States, south of the White Mountains.\n- Squam Lake straddles the borders of Grafton County, Carroll County, and Belknap County.\n- The Pratt Family Camps consist of three primary camp houses and a collection of outbuildings.\n- The Pratt family constructed the buildings at Pratt Family Camps over an 85-year period.\n- Pratt Family Camps occupy more than 80 acres of lakefront property on Squam Lake.",
